            <ArticleTitle>A subdural abscess and infected blood patch complicating regional analgesia for labour.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>246-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two very unusual cases of infection complicating labour analgesia. The first case was a sub-dural abscess presenting with deep-seated backache seven days after combined spinal-epidural analgesia for labour. The second was a painful lumbar swelling and septicaemia that presented three days after a blood patch for a post dural puncture headache. Because of their complicated and unusual presentation, the diagnosis and management of both were initially delayed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
